  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2023 Workplace First Aid Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NLRC has provided structured investment (including a contribution to the running costs) and technical support for ZRCS&#x2019; workplace first aid business from 2017-2021. In 2022 and 2023 ZRCS took on 100% of the running costs of the business, whilst NLRC still provided technical support where needed and supported specific investments into the business. The level of business growth in the past few years has exceeded expectations &#x2013; including during the period of Covid when business activity was suppressed. Over the 7 years since investment began, the WFA business turnover has grown on average by 25% a year (this is compound level of growth), generating approximately 210k Euros in revenue in 2022, and 80k Euros surplus (av. 2022 exchange rate). The surplus funds have enabled ZRCS to take more control of their financial situation, to resolve debts, facilitate NS investment and development, and fulfil more of their humanitarian ambition. Market knowledge indicates that there is further growth to be found &#x2013; many companies and organisations do not purchase first aid training, other competitors are growing in different markets, existing customers are requesting additional training products from ZRCS, and the government is very keen to develop a training system for new drivers. In 2022 NLRC provided funding to allow the WFA business to innovate and take risks &#x2013; with support for a professional level advertising campaign. In 2023, NLRC continued this approach of financially supporting innovation and risk through support for the development of new advertising mediums and new product development. NLRC is separately supporting the development of a new training centre through the MoFA grant. At the same time ZRCS will continue taking financial responsibility for the running costs of the business so any new ventures will not affect the core business.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through technical support and financial support to innovation through support for the development of new advertising mediums and new product development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the further growth of the WFA business, and therefore the financial sustainability of the ZRCS.</narrative>
  </description>
